        "acc_usage": {
          "type": "aurora_accordion",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How to use",
            "kind": "content",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>Light all sides of the rim for 20 seconds, keep the flame for 20 more seconds, then let it glow amber. Sprinkle the herbal powder on the ember for a richer aroma.</p>"
          }
        },
        "acc_inside": {
          "type": "aurora_accordion",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What's inside",
            "kind": "content",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p><strong>Purified desi cow dung</strong> – the natural, charcoal-free base that burns clean.<br/><strong>Sacred herbs & resins</strong> – sandalwood, frankincense, myrrh, benzoin (Dasangam blend).<br/><strong>Hydro-distilled Paneer Rose</strong> – a soft floral note (Floral variant).<br/><strong>Lemongrass extract</strong> – fresh citrus that also keeps insects away (Lemongrass variant).</p><p>No charcoal · No bamboo · No synthetic fragrance · No chemical binders</p>",
            "metafield_key": "combo_includes"
          }
        },
        "acc_cowdung": {
          "type": "aurora_accordion",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is cow dung incense?",
            "kind": "content",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>For centuries, Indian homes have burned dried desi cow dung (gomaya) in yagnas and homams to purify the air. Aurora uses the same purified, solar-dried cow dung – mixed with herbs, resins and natural extracts – instead of charcoal and bamboo.</p><p>It is <strong>odourless once dried</strong>, burns slowly and evenly, and leaves an ash you can use as vibhuti or plant fertiliser. Every purchase also supports cow welfare and rescue.</p>"
          }
        },
        "acc_compare": {
          "type": "aurora_accordion",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Aurora vs regular incense",
            "kind": "comparison",
            "open": false,
            "brand_label": "Aurora",
            "other_label": "Regular incense",
            "rows": "Base material | Purified desi cow dung | Charcoal powder\nBamboo core | None – bamboo-less | Bamboo stick core\nFragrance | Natural herbs & extracts | Synthetic perfume\nChemical binders | None | Often used\nEye irritation / heavy smoke | Gentle, low smoke | Common\nLeftover ash | Reusable as fertiliser / vibhuti | Waste\nSafe around kids & pets | Yes | Not always"
          }
        },
        "acc_shipping": {
          "type": "aurora_accordion",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Shipping & returns",
            "kind": "content",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p><strong>Shipping:</strong> Dispatched within 3–5 working days. FREE shipping on orders above ₹999; a flat ₹60 applies below ₹999.</p><p><strong>Returns:</strong> Damaged or unusable products are replaced free when reported within <strong>24 hours of delivery</strong> (share an unboxing photo/video on WhatsApp). Orders cannot be cancelled or exchanged for change of mind.</p>"
          }
        },
        "acc_faq": {
          "type": "aurora_accordion",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Honest answers to common questions",
            "kind": "faq",
            "open": false,
            "question_1": "Does cow dung incense smell of dung?",
            "answer_1": "<p>No. The cow dung is purified and solar-dried, so it is odourless. You only smell the herbs, resins and natural extracts.</p>",
            "question_2": "Are these safe for children, elders and pets?",
            "answer_2": "<p>Yes. Aurora is made with natural, chemical-free ingredients and no synthetic binders. As with any incense, burn it in a ventilated space.</p>",
            "question_3": "How long does each stick or cup burn?",
            "answer_3": "<p>Sticks burn for about 45 minutes; cups for about 25–30 minutes. The aroma lingers for hours.</p>",
            "question_4": "How do I light an incense cup?",
            "answer_4": "<p>Light all sides of the rim for 20 seconds, keep the flame for 20 more seconds, then let it glow amber. Sprinkle the herbal powder on the ember for a richer aroma.</p>",
            "question_5": "Which one should I start with?",
            "answer_5": "<p>Sticks are perfect for daily use; cups give a deeper, temple-like aroma. If you are new, a combo pack lets you try both.</p>",
            "question_6": "What can I do with the leftover ash?",
            "answer_6": "<p>Use it as vibhuti, mix it into plant soil as a natural fertiliser, or use it to scrub utensils.</p>",
            "question_7": "What are the shipping charges and delivery time?",
            "answer_7": "<p>Orders ship in 3–5 working days. Shipping is FREE above ₹999; a flat ₹60 applies below that.</p>",
            "question_8": "What if my order arrives damaged?",
            "answer_8": "<p>Send us a photo or unboxing video on WhatsApp within 24 hours of delivery and we will replace it free.</p>"
          }
        },
        "acc_safety": {
          "type": "aurora_accordion",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Safety & disclaimer",
            "kind": "content",
            "open": false,
            "content": "<p>Never leave burning incense unattended. Burn on a heat-proof holder in a ventilated room, away from curtains, paper and anything flammable, and out of reach of children and pets. Not for consumption.</p><p>As a handmade natural product, colour, aroma and burn time may vary slightly from batch to batch.</p>"
          }
        },
